    "updated_at": "2020-06-23T10:55:14Z",
    "body": "> High performance applications try to avoid creating temporaries to reduce GC impact.\r\n\r\nIs there a reason why the JS engines can't do escape analysis and heap-allocate temporary view objects? Is there a reason why the nursery in the GC doesn't take care of this?",
